{"kind":"propose","text":"Adopt a signed, fold-enforced `reassign_if_unclaimed` precondition so a reassignment cannot assert that a request is still unclaimed from an earlier read. The helper must encode the exact old request and, on the replacement, the effective retirement it follows; it must require the request to remain live and fresh with no admitted direct promise or direct completion/report. The retirement step checks that claim-free tuple before retiring; the replacement checks the same tuple still holds after the named retirement. If a promise or completion lands between those acts, the replacement refuses and tells the author to re-read instead of publishing a false diligence claim. Unrelated durable events must not refuse it.\n\nMake the condition authoritative in new signed Workroom schemas for guarded retirement and guarded replacement, with the fold as the final judge and the application post-dedup hook using the same rule for early refusal at the exact pre-sequence frontier. Unknown older folds must leave the new acts ineffective rather than grant them force; bump the fold profile. Do not reduce this to projected status strings: a retired request can still hide a late direct completion behind `withdrawn`. The condition is the exact commitment tuple/fingerprint: request, retirement where applicable, and absence of direct promise/completion.\n\nExpose this first as the purpose-specific helper in CLI and MCP so callers cannot compose the tuple incorrectly; ordinary supersede remains available for a requester deliberately withdrawing promised work. Document Layers 5 and 7 and the reassignment workflow. Tests must reproduce the #12760 retirement / #12761 promise / #12762 replacement order from dc3e7e73; prove promise-before-retirement refusal, promise-between-acts replacement refusal, unrelated interleaving acceptance, exact replay, malformed or ambiguous expectation failure, fold enforcement under an admission-skipping/older resident, and unchanged deliberate withdrawal authority. This is narrower and less noisy than a whole-frontier CAS, while remaining durable under binary skew."}